# Drafted by Gemini (R18 night), edited.

~ camp
Narrator: A hollow between great grey roots offers a dry patch of moss, though the air still tastes of cellar damp and old spores.
* Make camp for the night -> camp_chain
* Press on -> END

~ camp_chain
time +60
if not flag.hb_night_drums
set hb_night_drums
-> drums
elif not flag.hb_night_shadow
set hb_night_shadow
-> hartsblight/gorthos:shadow
elif not flag.hb_night_shriek
set hb_night_shriek
-> shriek
elif not flag.hb_night_dryad
set hb_night_dryad
-> hartsblight/dryad:dryad_arrive
else
Narrator: Nothing stirs beyond the firelight save the slow drip of grey dew from the fungal shelves, and you sleep until a pale, sunless morning.
-> END
endif

~ drums
Narrator: Low hide drums thump through the mist from a quarter-mile off, keeping a slow, wet pulse while several throats chant in the old tongue of the woods.
* Follow the drums -> drums_follow
* Leave them -> drums_leave

~ drums_follow
time +15
Narrator: You pick your way over slick roots toward the beat until torchlight glimmers on four antlered figures Hammering on skins stretched over hollow logs.
set hb_drums_followed
combat hb_drums

~ drums_leave
Narrator: The drumming dies away toward false dawn, and an hour later the ground trembles under a heavy, rotting tread crashing straight for your embers.
set hb_mammoth_woke
combat hb_mammoth

~ shriek
Narrator: From somewhere out in the dark, a couple of hundred yards through the mist, a young man's voice tears the night open, begging for help.
* [Perception DC 13] Find where it comes from -> shriek_found | shriek_lost
* [Insight DC 17] It is not a human voice -> shriek_notice | shriek_lost
* Go to him -> shriek_go
* Stay put -> shriek_stay

~ shriek_found
Narrator: The cry echoes off a ridge of dead, barkless pines just up the slope, where heavy shapes are snapping the lower boughs.
-> shriek

~ shriek_lost
Narrator: The fog and the thick shelving fungus scatter the sound until it seems to come from every hollow at once.
-> shriek

~ shriek_notice
Narrator: The cry repeats with the exact same catch in the throat and no breath taken between words, like a clacking beak repeating a trick.
set hb_heard_halden
set hb_screams_mimic
-> shriek_stay

~ shriek_go
Narrator: You push through the wet ferns toward the voice, and two feathered hulks with hooked beaks wheel around from a bare carcass in the gloom.
set hb_heard_halden
combat hb_owlbears

~ shriek_stay
Narrator: You keep low by the cold ashes until the screaming cuts off mid-syllable, and two heavy, feathered shapes lumber away through the brush.
set hb_heard_halden
if flag.hb_halden_journal
quest hb_halden_hunt traced
endif
-> END
